EXPLAIN PARALLEL EXECUTION IN PLAYWRIGHT *******************************

Playwright has built in parallel execution. No additional library or plugins needed. 
By default, playwright runs its tests in parallel across multiple worker processes. Each worker runs its tests independently in its own browser instance.

Each worker has its own browser context meaning there is no sharing of cookies, local storage, Authentication state , browser cache, session storage This is called ISOLATED CONTEXTS. There is no interference between parallel test executions. 

PW runs test files in parallel by default workers. However, if test files are there inside a single file..then these test files are run sequentially unless parallel execution is explicitly enabled by setting fullyparallel:true in playwright.config.ts 

